{
    "pageid": 27,
    "title": "Education",
    "sections": [
        {
            "heading": "Introduction",
            "level": 1,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Education is the process by which child character gains traits and attributes ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Each character in the game has a childhood up until the age of 16. During this period of time the character is educated in the ways of life, represented by the character gaining traits and attributes . Education in the base game happens in three stages:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ol",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Until the age of 6, the child's development is influenced by the primary parent. The primary character is decided by what type of marriage the child is a result of; if it is a patrilineal marriage the father is the primary parent, and if it is a matrilineal marriage the mother is the primary parent.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "At the age of 6, the assigned guardian takes over for nearly all purposes until the child comes of age at 16.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "At age 16, an education trait is assigned based on the final guardian's education trait.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Each adult can have up to two wards at a time.  Guardians have increased plot power against their wards for the purpose of assassination ."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "You will receive an alert when a child in your court age 6 or older is without a tutor."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "If you want to groom your grandson or a similar future heir is out of your control, you can ask to become their guardian on their sixth birthday.  If your offer is accepted you will thus have the opportunity to groom your future heir, or ensure that a potential rival ends up with horrible traits, thus eliminating that threat."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Culture and religion",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The child will often adopt the culture or religion of his tutor, hence the importance of guardian choice. This happens more often if the guardian is:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Diligent for both culture and religion,",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Zealous for religion,",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Gregarious for culture.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The opposite traits Slothful , Cynical and Shy have the opposite effect."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "However, these events will not happen if the tutor is not of the same culture or religion as their employer (landed nobles are their own employers)."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Base attributes",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "One of the things a parent/guardian will affect is base attributes.  It appears that each child has a chance once per year to increase each of their base attributes.  The chance that an increase will occur is tied to the attribute of the parent/guardian."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Thus, a child will gain base attributes more quickly in an area the parent/guardian is skilled at than one which he/she's bad at. Thus children will often end up with a distribution of base attributes quite similar to their parent or guardian.  This also means it can be more important to have a strong distribution of attributes in an heir's guardian/mentor, rather than one exceptionally strong attribute and very low other attributes."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "According to one player's testing, a statistic of 17 or above make the child very likely to gain a point in that same attribute."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Ultimately there is an element of random chance, however, so it is possible that a child will get a distribution of base attributes quite different from the parent/guardian."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Note that congenital traits (like quick or imbecile) seem to be reflected in the guardian's attributes and, therefore, increase / decrease the ward's chance to gain base attribute points."
                }
            ]
        },
