        {
            "heading": "Personality traits",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Personality traits are also gained during tutoring and help define the character. AI guardians will generally encourage their wards to have traits similar to their own, while players acting as guardians are mostly free to guide wards in any chosen direction."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Some traits that affect AI guardians are:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "very good: Diligent , Kind , and Temperate guardians make good choices in many events.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "good: Just guardians make good choices, and Proud guardians stay out of the way when the child is doing well naturally.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "mediocre: Zealous guardians are good at making children Zealous, but leave almost everything else up to chance.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "bad: Gluttonous , Arbitrary , Cruel , Wroth , and Craven",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "terrible: Slothful",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "For detailed calculations, see Evaluation of guardian traits ."
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Effects on guardians",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Many events have options with effects on guardians:"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Lose zealous or cynical , by approving of a child gaining the opposite trait",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Gain 5 piety by choosing religious options such as praying (requires not being cynical )",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Lose 5 prestige by encouraging a child to have certain traits opposite from your own",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Many events allow skilled guardians to improve ward stats, but a handful allow skilled guardians to improve their own stats :"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "When a child naturally gains honest or kind , the guardian can gain 1 diplomacy if already 10+",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "When a child naturally gains patient , the guardian can gain 1 intrigue if already 10+",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Each event can only fire if the child does not have the trait or its opposite",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Each event can only fire if the child has fewer than 5 personality traits",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Each event is 10x more likely to fire for genius children, and 2x more likely to fire for quick or weak children.",
                            "children": []
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "heading": "Strategies",
            "level": 2,
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Choose guardians based on the stats and traits you want each character to have :"
                },
                {
                    "type": "list",
                    "list_type": "ul",
                    "items": [
                        {
                            "text": "Your heir should be a likable ruler with strong stats.",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "The same applies to your heir's heir, or anyone you might choose as an heir .",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Vassals should be Content , share your culture, and share positive personality traits with your heir.",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Bear in mind that this is not always desirable: If your authority is low enough and you want your vassals to expand on their own, content ones are less likely to do it.",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Claimants on your titles should be managed carefully, lest they become adventurers or gain faction support.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Dynastic claimants on foreign realms should be encouraged to become adventurers , so you can join their war and gain an ally.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Future cardinals and antipopes should be virtuous, pious, and generally likable.",
                            "children": []
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Future council members should be strong in their primary attribute.",
                            "children": [
                                {
                                    "text": "Future spymasters should also have high ai_honor so they don't help murder your kids, but this tends to conflict with having high intrigue skill...",
                                    "children": []
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Educate heir yourself : you have much better control over a child's personality this way than by choosing a guardian. Once the child has 5 personality traits, you can safely send them to another tutor for better stats or education trait. (this is no longer a guarantee, there have been reports of a 6th, or even 7th trait before the age of 16)"
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Always have two wards : choices in the events can help your character, especially if you don't care about the child's well-being."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Look for guardians with Tier 4 education traits : having such a tutor in the last year gives the child a good chance to pick up the same education, for +9 in one stat and +2 in two others."
                },
                {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "If you pick a guardian outside your own court, be careful with guardians of other religions/cultures , unless you actually want to switch religion/culture. If both the guardian and the owner of the court the guardian is in (the same person if the guardian themself is landed) is of a different culture/religion, your child may switch. Note that if you are a child, you can choose to avoid the culture- and religion-changing events, so you can have a different-culture guardian without danger of being unwillingly converted."
                },
